{"slug":"surrey-council-to-vote-on-34m-intersection-improvements-8819466","path":"/blog.html/surrey-council-to-vote-on-34m-intersection-improvements-8819466","url":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/surrey-council-to-vote-on-34m-intersection-improvements-8819466","kind":"blog","title":"Surrey Council to Vote on $3.4M Intersection Improvements","canonical":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/surrey-council-to-vote-on-34m-intersection-improvements-8819466","seo":{"Title":"Surrey Council to Vote on $3.4M Intersection Improvements","Meta description":"Surrey council to decide on $3.4M contract for intersection upgrades at King George Blvd & 108 Ave and 148 St & 16 Ave, plus consulting agreements.","H1":"Surrey Council to Vote on $3.4M Intersection Upgrades in North & South Surrey","Canonical":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/surrey-council-to-vote-on-34m-intersection-improvements-8819466","Meta robots":"","OG title":"Surrey Council to Vote on $3.4M Intersection Upgrades in North & South Surrey","OG description":"Surrey council to decide on $3.4M contract for intersection upgrades at King George Blvd & 108 Ave and 148 St & 16 Ave, plus consulting agreements.","OG image":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/wps/rest/64736/blog/kicc/kicctivmlsei.jpg","Published":"2025-09-30T00:19:55+00:00","Modified":"2025-09-30T00:24:24+00:00"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"RSS","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.feed"}]},{"t":"h","level":1,"text":"Surrey Council to Vote on $3.4M Intersection Upgrades in North & South Surrey"},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Posted on"},{"t":"September 29, 2025"},{"t":"by"},{"t":"Jared Gibbons","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/about.html"}],"cls":"byline"},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Surrey’s road network","h":"https://www.surrey.ca/"},{"t":"could soon see major improvements as city council votes tonight on a new package of intersection upgrades in both North and South Surrey."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"A corporate report from Scott Neuman, Surrey’s general manager of engineering, recommends awarding a"},{"t":"$3,395,516.25 contract to Crown Contracting Ltd."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"for construction. Council will also be asked to set a spending limit of"},{"t":"$3,651,067.88"},{"t":"to cover the full scope of work at two key intersections:"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"King George Boulevard and 108 Avenue","h":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/King+George+Blvd+%26+108+Ave,+Surrey,+BC+V3T+2X6,+Canad%C3%A1/@49.1988019,-122.8460331,17z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x5485d7867bf2fbaf:0x2ffc421980eff5e8!8m2!3d49.1988019!4d-122.8460331!16s%2Fg%2F11f3bq4z5w?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI1MDkyNC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D"},{"t":"in North Surrey, and"},{"t":"148 Street and 16 Avenue","h":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/148+St+%26+16+Ave,+Surrey"},{"t":"in South Surrey."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Along with the primary construction contract, staff recommend additional consulting agreements."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"McElhanney Ltd."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"would receive"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"$92,961.75 (limit $102,260)"},{"t":"for the north project, while"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"R.F. Binnie & Associates Ltd."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"would be awarded"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"$39,406.50 (limit $43,350)"},{"t":"for the south project."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"At"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"King George Boulevard and 108 Avenue"},{"t":", improvements include dual northbound and southbound left-turn lanes to reduce congestion, as well as a redesigned pedestrian island to shorten crossing distances and improve sightlines for turning vehicles. The project also incorporates utility coordination, including installation of ducting for undergrounding"},{"t":"BC Hydro 3-phase wiring","h":"https://www.bchydro.com/index.html"},{"t":"to support"},{"t":"City Centre’s ongoing beautification efforts","h":"https://www.surrey.ca/about-surrey/our-communities/city-centre"},{"t":"."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Meanwhile, the"},{"t":"148 Street and 16 Avenue"},{"t":"project will rebuild the traffic signal to enhance traffic flow and safety. If approved, construction will run from"},{"t":"7 a.m. to 10 p.m., Monday through Friday"},{"t":", starting in October and scheduled for completion by February."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"These upgrades mark another step in Surrey’s commitment to easing congestion, improving safety, and investing in infrastructure for a growing city."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"📞 Want to learn more about Surrey’s latest infrastructure upgrades and how they may impact local real estate?"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Contact Jared Gibbons today","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/contact.html"},{"t":"to get expert insights and guidance."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Blogs"},{"t":"All Blog Posts","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html"}]},{"t":"list","items":[[{"t":"New Listings","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html?blog=86690"}],[{"t":"Open Houses","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html?blog=86691"}],[{"t":"Real Estate Blog","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html?blog=82607"}],[{"t":"Sold Listings","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html?blog=86692"}]]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Posts By Date"},{"t":"Most Recent","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html"}]},{"t":"list","items":[[{"t":"October 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/10/"}],[{"t":"September 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/09/"}],[{"t":"August 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/08/"}],[{"t":"July 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/07/"}],[{"t":"June 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/06/"}],[{"t":"May 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/05/"}],[{"t":"April 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/04/"}],[{"t":"March 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html